# Repository-wide text normalization.
#
# VAC targets Windows too, but source, docs, configs, tests, and web assets are
# kept as UTF-8 text with LF line endings. This avoids CRLF/LF churn across
# Windows, WSL, CI, and generated GUI fixtures.
#
# PowerShell scripts can also use LF. If a future .ps1 must support Windows
# PowerShell 5.1 and contains non-ASCII literals, prefer documenting that script
# as UTF-8 with BOM separately instead of changing the whole repository policy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets.
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
